- **`godot/effects/jump_puff.tscn`**: a `JumpPuff` root (`Node2D`) with three `CPUParticles2D` children, `Flash`, `Puff` and `Specks`. Every value from the A3 table is written out in the scene. All three emitters share one `GradientTexture2D` defined inside the scene. There's no script, no draw material and no image file.
- **`godot/tests/test_jump_puff_config.gd`**: loads the scene and reads back every setting A3 names, comparing each to the brief's value. It also checks that no emitter has a fixed seed or `preprocess`.
- **`godot/previews/jump_puff_preview.tscn`** and its script **`jump_puff_preview.gd`**:
  - It loads the real level (`main.tscn`) and leaves it in the menu, so nothing moves and Extinguisho stays off screen at the spawn.
  - It points the game's own camera at (1205, 180), where the game puts it when he stands at x 1105.
  - It hides the HUD, because in the menu its card and dark tint would cover the art.
  - It adds a puff to the level node at (1105, 280) on frame 10, and again on frame 25 when `retrigger` is on. Each puff gets fixed seeds.

All property names are the Godot 4.7.2 ones, already confirmed by `a6/evidence/probes/names_probe.log`. I'm not unsure about any of them. One limit: the test can't prove Godot accepted the `local_coords = false` line, because false is also the default. The name itself is confirmed by the probe.

